<title>USA: Campbell sells poultry unit, closes 3 plants.</title>
<headline>Campbell sells poultry unit, closes 3 plants.</headline>
<dateline>CAMDEN, N.J. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Campbell Soup Co said Wednesday it has sold its poultry operations to Wayne Farms, a division of Continental Grain Co, for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>The company said it also has closed three tomato-paste plants and sold its Argentina beef ranches.</p>
<p>Campbell said the moves are part of a cost-productivity initiative announced last September designed to generate $200 million in savings through 1998.</p>
</text>
